  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 2.30.102 - AM033 distinguishes concrete converter usage from interface fallback\n- An interface-typed local with a concrete initializer marks only that implementation as used\n- Unused sibling converters for the same source and destination pair now report\n- Same-block data flow preserves broad fallback after local reassignment\n- Mutable, constructor-injected, and service-located interface handles remain conservative when no stable concrete implementation is statically traceable\n- No rule ID or severity changes",
